                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "34872904-83d6-3870-aaeb-80a9c6d00097",
                        "entry_id": "9af5bcc2-1f73-32b8-9630-3cd0872ef065",
                        "glosses": [
                            "анат. наружная плотная белковая оболочка глаза, в передней части переходящая в роговицу"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "06ec0c39-f9d7-4245-b6cc-fad545f2eb0a",
                                "sense_id": "34872904-83d6-3870-aaeb-80a9c6d00097",
                                "text": "У некоторых людей от природы слабая наружная оболочка глазного яблока (склера). Она не может сдержать рост глаза. Работа на близком расстоянии (чтение, письмо, работа за компьютером) способствует этому росту, а значит, развивается близорукость."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "365e1177-7f8b-4c3d-9a0f-049232e4b692",
                        "source_entry_id": "9af5bcc2-1f73-32b8-9630-3cd0872ef065",
                        "source_sense_id": "34872904-83d6-3870-aaeb-80a9c6d00097",
                        "target_lang_word": "sclera",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sclera",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "390f4410-d999-3afb-969b-a0122dc4b55f",
                                        "entry_id": "31b7f8cc-6451-3c5c-9eb3-5c5b42ec9adc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The white of the eye; the tough outer coat of the eye that covers the eyeball except for the cornea."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "baabfeb4-4e80-4978-af39-751fe3d67408",
                                                "sense_id": "390f4410-d999-3afb-969b-a0122dc4b55f",
                                                "text": "She'd been back a week and it was clear that college-level track was kicking her ass, the sclera in her normally wide manga-eyes were shot through with blood vessels."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac0f1607-d42d-4165-a9ea-7a4abbb5847e",
                                                "sense_id": "390f4410-d999-3afb-969b-a0122dc4b55f",
                                                "text": "Such pressures explain why humans are peculiar in having our rather small irises set against a white background—the sclera—in our eyes. Anyone watching us can infer where we are looking or whom we are looking at."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7de1165a-f649-4dd2-9e1f-d2db3cc3161e",
                        "source_entry_id": "9af5bcc2-1f73-32b8-9630-3cd0872ef065",
                        "source_sense_id": "34872904-83d6-3870-aaeb-80a9c6d00097",
